; Regression: a non-ASCII character inside or before a name produced K0100/K0102/K0125 on top
; of the lexer's K0001, and the rest of the line became junk. As in grammar.md §19.4
; (`struct Café {}` dumps as `(StructDecl struct Caf (ErrorNode é) (MemberList))`), the Error
; token is wrapped where it occurs and parsing continues as if it were not there.
(SourceFile
  (FieldDecl let caf (ErrorNode é) = (Literal 1))
  (FieldDecl let (ErrorNode ​) b = (Literal 2)))
